(This technical document formalizes the autonomous lunar landing hazard detection, slope quantification, and candidate touchdown site selection) Tj
T* (methodology implemented in LunarSafe. Lunar landing safe zones require strict topography tolerances to avoid mechanical lander tip-over, chassis) Tj
T* (structural collapse, or propulsion plume re-impingement. LunarSafe establishes a fully deterministic, zero-hallucination processing pipeline capable of) Tj
T* (ingesting high-resolution planetary data from NASA LOLA digital elevation models \(Float32 rasters\) and ISRO Chandrayaan-2/3 Terrain Mapping Camera 2) Tj
T* (\(TMC-2\) and Orbiter High Resolution Camera \(OHRC\) panchromatic products. The core engine applies Horn's \(1981\) third-order finite difference operator) Tj
T* (with 8*GSD stencil weighting for genuine physical slope quantification, accompanied by first-order analytical error propagation that models altimetric laser) Tj
T* (error \(sigma_z = 1.0m\) to enforce a conservative 2-sigma safety filter. Candidate terrain is partitioned into standard 24m x 24m ISRO landing grid cells,) Tj
T* (ensuring verifiable compliance with ISRO LHDAC mission thresholds \(slope <= 10.0 deg, crater depth <= 1.0m, boulder height <= 0.30m\). All computational) Tj
T* (decisions are bound to an immutable 5-stage SHA-256 evidence chain, guaranteed by Ed25519 digital signatures and AES-256-GCM encryption for) Tj
T* (complete post-flight mission auditability.) Tj
ET
