0.176 0.216 0.282 rg
39.6850393700787407 565.5120472440944468 Td
(The terminal descent of a lunar lander represents one of the most mission-critical phases in planetary exploration. In September 2019, the Chandrayaan-2) Tj
T* (Vikram lander experienced an off-nominal trajectory deviation during its fine-braking phase. Subsequent failure analysis conducted by the National Expert) Tj
T* (Committee identified that tight thruster throttling limits combined with unexpected trajectory dispersion forced the guidance system to attempt rapid attitude) Tj
T* (corrections, resulting in high horizontal velocity at touchdown beyond the capability of the landing legs. This historic failure highlighted the paramount) Tj
T* (necessity of onboard autonomous real-time hazard detection with absolute determinism, wide safe-zone search radii, and mathematically bounded) Tj
T* (uncertainty margins.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7.5 Tf
8.625 TL
0.176 0.216 0.282 rg
39.6850393700787407 497.1970866141732017 Td
(LunarSafe addresses this challenge by providing pre-landing terrain qualification and onboard hazard map synthesis. Unlike deep learning black-box models) Tj
T* (that suffer from stochastic unpredictability and out-of-distribution hallucinations under varying solar illumination, LunarSafe relies on closed-form geometric) Tj
T* (algorithms that produce 100% bit-identical results across all computing platforms.) Tj
