(1. NASA LOLA Gridded Data Record \(GDR\): Single-band IEEE 754 Float32 raster representing topocentric elevation in meters relative to the reference) Tj
T* (lunar sphere \(R = 1737.4 km\). Typical resolution ranges from 20.0m \(polar tiles\) to 59.225m \(equatorial maria\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7.5 Tf
8.625 TL
0.176 0.216 0.282 rg
39.6850393700787407 235.2758267716533283 Td
(2. ISRO Chandrayaan-2/3 TMC-2 & OHRC: Planetary Data System version 4 \(PDS4\) standard format comprising an XML label \(*.xml\) and an) Tj
T* (uncompressed 16-bit Little-Endian \(UnsignedLSB2\) raw raster \(*.img\). Raster line and sample counts are parsed dynamically from the PDS4 label to) Tj
T* (prevent geometry mismatches across instruments. The bug was a dynamic-range assumption error. The loader divided raw pixel values by 65,535, but the) Tj
T* (sensor's actual dynamic range for this observation was only ~9–455. This crushed all pixels to near-zero, producing a blank image. The fix applies a 2-sigma) Tj
T* (dynamic-range stretch with gamma correction \(gamma = 0.43\), computed from the tile's actual mean and standard deviation.) Tj
